response_content_full:
The sauce volume is half of the original canned‑tomato volume (the tomatoes lose half their volume when cooked).

1. **Find the original canned‑tomato volume needed**  
   \\[
   \\text{Original volume} = 2 \\times \\text{sauce volume}
   = 2 \\times 32\\text{ oz}
   = 64\\text{ oz}
   \\]

2. **Convert that volume to number of cans**  
   Each can holds 16 oz, so  
   \\[
   \\text{Number of cans} = \\frac{64\\text{ oz}}{16\\text{ oz/can}} = 4\\text{ cans}
   \\]

3. **Find the total number of tomatoes**  
   Each can contains 3 tomatoes, so  
   \\[
   \\text{Total tomatoes} = 4\\text{ cans} \\times 3\\text{ tomatoes/can} = 12\\text{ tomatoes}
   \\]

\\[
\\boxed{12}
\\]

